# Everything by default; the Dockerfile opts in to what it needs. An allowlist
# cannot leak a file nobody thought to exclude — and `.env` is the file that
# would otherwise get baked into a layer, where it persists even if a later
# layer deletes it (docs/backend/13-deployment.md#container-design).
*

!Backend/package.json
!Backend/package-lock.json
!Backend/src
!Backend/test
!ops

# Re-excluded inside the allowed paths.
**/node_modules
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/*.log
**/.DS_Store
